WEBVTT

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.980
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.340
I want to ask if you've seen a flower
like this in the forest anywhere.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.800
Help me!

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.330
Ever since we found that flower,

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.200
there have been terrifying sounds
every night!

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.210
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.970
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:17.870
What are you doing?!

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.810
-Fire! Fire!
-Somebody! Help me!

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:31.110
CHAPTER 20

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:36.020
MEMORIES OF THE YOKA

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.680
Yes?

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.580
Yes, this is.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.590
What? Aunt Toshiko...?!

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.800
She collapsed outside?

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.590
That's pretty close.
I'll go check up on her.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.140
What is it?

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.850
Mana, you're free, right?

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.980
I have my summer homework!

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:58.270
I can't decide what to do
for my research project.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.000
Then you're free.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:04.000
Aunt Toshiko in Chiba?

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.510
She's your grandmother's older sister,
so she's actually your great-aunt.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.320
She's a bit of a black sheep
among our relatives,

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:19.020
but she took a liking to me for
some reason, and was always good to me.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.130
What are you here for?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:25.150
Nobody asked you to come.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.150
You seem well.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.890
Shouldn't you be lying down?

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:33.780
You hit 90 and things start breaking down.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.720
TOSHIKO SAWADA

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.850
It's a fact of life.
Everyone should leave me alone.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.310
Now, now.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.150
Mana, was it?

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:44.770
Yes...

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.320
She's gotten big, hasn't she?

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.450
Are you studying hard?

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.950
Huh? Uh... Sort of.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.720
"Sort of " what?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.060
I hate it when people can't give
a straight answer.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:03.290
Give me a simple "yes" or "no"!

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:05.350
Uh, yes!

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:06.960
Very good.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.860
I'll go get you a change of clothes.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.850
I can do it myself, but no one listens.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.600
Don't trouble your doctors too much.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:21.730
I've lived this long by myself.
I'm perfectly ready to kick the bucket.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:25.370
Sure. But we'd miss you,
so hold on a little longer.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.690
Is there anything you want
or need me to do?

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:38.680
It's almost <i>obon</i> season.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.470
The flowers...

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:46.060
Will you check on the flowers?

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:54.850
How many years has it been?
I've missed this.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.180
I'd stopped coming here.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.660
Plus, Aunt Toshiko isn't really
a people person.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.760
Hmm...

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.080
I can't find any relevant records.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.880
Nanashi... If he really has no name,
there's no way to research him...

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.070
Why don't you take a break?

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:34.300
Ah, some refreshments.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.180
Thanks, Catchick.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.890
It's nothing.
Sand Witch asked me to bring these.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.270
Have you been
keeping touch with Mana-chan?

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.330
What's going on?

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:49.070
She seems to frequently get involved
in Nanashi incidents.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:52.360
We should probably keep tabs on her.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:56.010
Speak of the devil.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.430
Huh? What is this?

00:05:58.740 --> 00:05:59.510
Hmm?

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.050
Huh?

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:03.040
Hmm...

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.330
Are these...?

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.540
Hmm...

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:12.130
Red flowers... Red flowers...

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.190
These are all different.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.720
There's nothing on the internet.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:21.600
I looked in an encyclopedia once,
but I never found anything.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.450
Huh?

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:26.810
Whenever <i>obon</i> season comes around,
they always suddenly bloom.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:30.320
But I've never seen so many before.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.020
Oh really?

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.340
Oh?

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:37.610
A photo?

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.370
This is Aunt Toshiko.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:43.970
Huh. Who's the guy with her?

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.970
WITH SOUJIRO-SAN
1942

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.630
It's probably Aunt Toshiko's sweetheart.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:50.880
Her sweetheart?

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.840
I heard about him.

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:59.130
When Aunt Toshiko was young,
she fell in love with a man from Tokyo.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.340
They even promised to marry.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.120
But...

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:11.610
One day, he suddenly disappeared.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.190
He just said, "I promise I'll be back."

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:18.710
Aunt Toshiko waited,
believing those words.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:24.220
But he never showed up again.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:30.750
Since then, she felt she couldn't
love or be loved by anyone.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:36.610
She's lived alone
to this day believing that.

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:41.800
That guy just disappeared?
That's horrible!

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.310
True.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:48.850
But, this Soujiro-san might have had
some reason why.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:54.690
1942 means the war had already started.

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:57.610
The war?

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:03.660
You came all the way here?

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:06.250
These two were interested
in these flowers.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.010
Then, they're <i>yokai</i> related or something?

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:12.670
These are called yoka.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:16.000
They're flowers that bloom from
<i>yokai</i> activity or spirit power.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.920
So why are they at Aunt Toshiko's house?

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.550
I don't sense any malicious presence.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:27.450
It looks like these flowers
came from the south.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.890
Someplace very far away.

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:33.940
We should check it out.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:43.950
The flowers...

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:49.030
Will you check on the flowers?

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:54.710
If we're traveling, we'll need to prepare.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:56.840
Yes. We'll head out tomorrow morning.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:57.920
Okay.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.350
It's a clam boat.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.720
And the ferryman is Kawauso.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:10.410
It's much faster than it looks!

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.020
Are you really coming with us?

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.650
I want to know about those flowers.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:19.990
As promised,
I got permission from my parents.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.570
I said it's for my research project.

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:23.860
Good grief...

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.700
She's a good kid. That's nice.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:26.800
Why are you here?

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:27.870
I'm bored.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:30.290
Don't get in our way, or else.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:32.160
Okay, we're off!

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:04.030
It's this island. I'm sure of it.

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:08.120
It's hot. We've come pretty south.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.990
We've just crossed
the equator it looks like.

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:14.260
The red flowers came
all the way from here?

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:19.920
Huh?

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.170
IN MEMORIAM

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.250
This is... Japanese?!

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.110
KITARO'S TREE HOUSE

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:33.620
SHIGERU MIZUKI'S PARADISE
PAPUA NEW GUINEA

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:32.550
-<i>"Scratch, scratch."</i>
-<i>"Ge."</i>

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:33.560
<i>"Shake, shake."</i>

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:35.620
Japanese...

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:38.620
Why in a place so far away?

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.750
This is a monument to fallen soldiers.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:43.780
Huh?

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.820
Japanese soldiers fought on
this island during the war.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.990
And many died.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.450
The war...

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.720
The Pacific War.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.270
Didn't you learn about it at school?

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:03.510
I've heard about it.
But why on an island so far south?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:07.180
Long ago, Japan tried to expand.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.300
Against America, England, France...

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:14.270
Japan fought with countries
it considers friends now.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:18.400
It's probably hard for someone
of your generation to believe, Mana-chan.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:21.040
Man, it really was a crummy time.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:22.400
<i>Namu namu</i>...

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:27.300
I knew we went to war with America,

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:32.410
but, I thought it was like
Japan just got invaded and lost.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:37.680
No, Japan also invaded
and fought in other countries.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:40.460
Such an age really happened.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:44.130
It's been over 70 years.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:48.050
I suppose the memories
of war are fading...

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:53.990
This is...

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:56.600
Whew! Walking should be easier here!

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:57.700
But, something's...

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:01.690
KARIMARU FORESTY CO., LTD

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:00.850
Japanese again.

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:03.750
Rare trees go for high prices.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:08.990
So I hear some businesses go
all the way overseas to cut them down.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:12.490
We've got the proper permissions here.

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:18.240
We're not trying to
disrupt your work or anything.

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:23.140
I want to ask if you've seen a flower
like this in the forest anywhere.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:30.130
It's not my fault! It's not my fault!
I'm just doing my job!

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:30.970
This flower--

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.340
I don't know!

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:33.720
That look of terror...

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:36.910
Something’s cursed you, hasn’t it?

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:38.410
Talk to me.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:43.650
The <i>yokai</i> consultant for any supernatural
phenomenon, the BiBiBi no Rat Man,

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.730
and his merry companions are here to help.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.450
Help me!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.960
Ever since we found that flower,

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:56.590
there have been terrifying sounds
in the forest every night!

00:12:57.850 --> 00:13:00.540
Now we don't have to
wander the jungle all night.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.100
That was out of line.

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.920
Well, I'm curious about
that so-called "sound."

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:08.350
Mana, what's wrong?

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:11.440
It just hasn't really sunk in...

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:16.190
Right now, I'm far away from Japan,

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:21.370
where long ago, lots of
Japanese people came and fought...

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:24.480
And, even now...

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:29.270
They're doing it because there's a demand.
It's the principle of capitalism.

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:32.740
That's not what I wanted to talk about.

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.990
Where are you going?

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.660
I thought I'd get some water.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.010
I can do that.

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:40.800
It's fine! Don't follow! Got it?!

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:44.080
Can't he tell that I have to pee?

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:12.500
A-An air raid?!

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:15.010
Charge!

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:17.830
Hmm.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:21.330
I can't see any flashes of explosions
or gunfire anywhere.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.890
There's no vibrations or blast waves.
No smell of gunpowder either.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:28.750
It's really just the sound.

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:29.880
Hmm...

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:34.670
But, these are definitely
the sounds of war.

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:40.260
Please do something!
Every night these terrifying noises...!

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:43.370
The Tubuan! It's a curse of the Tubuan!

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:44.560
The Tubuan?

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:49.100
It's because we cut the forest
and tried to disturb the sacred tree!

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:50.980
The sacred tree?

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:52.920
You're hiding something shady.

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:54.190
Dad.

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:56.070
Hmm. The Tubuan...

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:59.430
Kitaro! I can't find Mana anywhere!

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:04.100
What are you doing?!

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:06.330
-Fire! Fire!
-Hold on! Don't die!

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:08.100
What... What is this?!

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:17.400
It's not doing anything?

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.590
It's just following me?

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:23.360
Maybe it's not a bad <i>yokai</i>.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:29.500
Oh, I know!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.460
Betobeto-san, go ahead.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:35.100
Was that it?

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:49.560
It's not disappearing.
Maybe it's not Betobeto-san.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:17:00.190
Does it want me to follow it somewhere?

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:35.730
Huh?

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:39.990
This is the source of the yoka.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.280
Kitaro!

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:44.390
You never cease to worry us.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.090
I'm sorry. I...

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:49.120
We know. It's all right.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.100
These are...

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.830
Remains of soldiers...

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:00.190
From their clothes,
they appear to be Japanese.

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:03.430
No one found them and they were left here.
<i>Namu namu</i>...

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:06.800
When we dug up the roots, we found these.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:10.930
We called the company and they said,
"Exporting the tree is a must.

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:13.980
If they're in the way,
just throw them away."

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:18.020
You'd throw away the remains of your
ancestors who fought for your country?!

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:19.320
How could you?!

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:22.990
Forgive us! We'll forget the tree!

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:28.240
The Tubuan took pity
and were protecting their remains.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:29.660
The Tubuan?

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:33.290
They're ancient spirits
that live in islands around here.

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:37.080
Normally, they won't harm people.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:41.980
They must have been intimidating
those who would disturb the remains.

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:47.970
They used their most
terrifying experience, the sounds of war.

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:55.520
Um, I know it's strange for me
to be saying this...

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:59.000
But, thank you very much!

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:11.410
Oh, what happened to those footprints?

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:12.570
Well?

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:13.970
Yes.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:16.970
The power that's creating the yoka...

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:20.170
This is its center.

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:21.710
A letter?

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:25.260
It's sealed and
doesn't look like it was ever sent.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.840
That dead guy must've written it.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:30.450
He got killed before he could send it.

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:33.640
Normally, paper should have
rotted away long ago.

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:36.270
A strong spirit power...

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:41.420
TOSHIKO SAWADA

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:43.580
SOUJIRO

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:53.430
Or a powerful feeling must have
taken root in it.

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:10.220
A feeling that he died
before he could say something.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:16.260
From there, the yoka were born,
and rode the winds far away to Japan.

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:21.040
This year's blooming must have been
a final message

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:24.350
because he sensed
this place would be lost.

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:27.230
I finally understand...

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:31.800
Lots of people really fought here.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:34.160
And died here...

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.480
<i>In the letter,</i>

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:48.590
<i>Soujiro-san wrote of how
his parents were strict about lineage</i>

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:50.840
<i>and wouldn't allow his marriage.</i>

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:56.520
<i>Soujiro-san didn't give up, angering them,
and he was forced to enlist in the army.</i>

00:20:56.520 --> 00:21:00.930
<i>Before he could send word,
he was sent to a far-away battlefield.</i>

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:07.380
<i>He wrote of so many things
that he hadn't been able to tell.</i>

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:08.520
<i>And...</i>

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:13.200
<i>"I promise I'll come home to you."</i>

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:13.260
I see.

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:18.120
He came back, just like he promised...

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:22.140
Thank you...

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:40.640
<i>War.</i>

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:44.620
<i>Long before we were born,</i>

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:46.190
<i>in a far-away place,</i>

00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:50.400
<i>there was a time when
many people killed and were killed.</i>

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:54.630
<i>We have to know about it.</i>

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:59.640
We can't allow ourselves
to forget about it.

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:05.080
ABOUT WAR
ABOUT PEACE

